    "description": "Natural Mineral Specimens\n13 Pound Geode and Crystal Collection\nAmethyst, Agate, Quartz, and Tumbled Stones\n13 lbs (Total Weight)\nNatural Geological Specimens\nThis diverse geological collection features approximately 13 pounds of natural mineral specimens. The lot includes high-quality amethyst clusters, polished banded agate slices, and hollow quartz geodes with sparkling crystalline interiors. Also present are various tumbled and raw stones such as tiger's eye, desert rose selenite, and rose quartz, representing a wide spectrum of geological formations and mineral types suitable for display, collection, or educational study.\nFeatures large amethyst druze specimens and polished banded agate slices\nIncludes a diverse variety of tumbled stones and raw mineral samples\nLargest specimens range from approximately 3 to 6 inches in size\nWeighs 13 lbs total for a substantial starting collection or bulk lot\nCondition:\nVery good natural condition. Specimens exhibit original rocky matrix and natural inclusions as expected with raw minerals. Polished pieces show smooth finishes, while geodes remain hollow with intact crystal structures. Minor age-appropriate wear to labels and natural geological fissures are present throughout the lot.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
